Z||000011||Mike Murphy||11-22-2001||09:28 PM||||The Washington Post article just about sums it up but since it was written we have lost, Bob Stemple, one of our best GM people that was an engineer who "was" CEO in the early 90's.  Bob unfortunately took over at a bad time and was forced to resign his position.<P>Too bad. He was the first car guy at the helm instead of a financial person in decades.<P>Anybody know what position Bill Hoglund is at presently?<P>Murph||||reg||14
