Z||000020||Old Lar||11-24-2001||05:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mike Murphy:<BR>[<P> Would you rather be the father of the Corvette, America's symbol of performance muscle car in several generations or the father of the Fiero, one of GM's best ideas but greatest failures.<P>Just be glad to own a piece of automotive history if you are lucky enough to own a Fiero.  They will only increase in value as time goes by.<P>Mike Murphy<BR>District Sales Manager <BR>Pontiac Motor Division<BR>1982-1987[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mike, I must take exception to the statement that the Fiero was one of GM's greatest failures.  I have one word... Vega.  Rated the second worst car ever made, and Monza (son of Vega). Cars made from compressed rust.  Vega, my first new car in 1972.<BR>There was also the Chevette, Astre, and the Fiero replacement: the Lemans.  Pontiac's recent disaster: the Astek.<P>I see no following of any sorts of those GM disaters.<P>GM's marketing is the disaster, GM's corporate culture is a disaster.  The only unique car GM produces is the Corvette, a limited production car that is in high demand, but unaffordable.||||reg||1
Z||000021||gtjeff||11-24-2001||07:07 PM||||I should mentioned that GM from what i have read didnt make a profit on Corvette until 1996 or 1997, yet it wasnt cancelled.<BR>Dont forget that Fiero outsold the "Overpriced One" every year 1984-88 (even with a 70% decrease in adv budget in 1988).<BR>In fact Fiero holds the sales record for 2 seaters in US for one model year. It should have had more corporate support for this reason.<BR>As far as Fiero RIP, you may want to go to the Detroit auto show, Bob Lutz responded to a forum members e-mail and made it sound like a fiero style car will be shown there.<BR>GM made a big mistake in canceling this car.<BR>After 2002 model year they will not have any affordable sports cars.<BR>It is kind of ironic but the next generation Corvette is rumored to be close in weight and size (maybe 6 inches longer) to a Fiero gt. They could have built that kind of car in '88.<BR>||||reg||1
